<Legal
  title="Research Use Disclaimer"
  description="The terms on which VIP Peptides supplies research materials, and the responsibilities accepted by the purchaser."
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <p class="lede">{RESEARCH_USE_NOTICE}</p>

  <h2>1. Nature of the products</h2>
  <p>
    All products supplied by {site.company.legalName} (&ldquo;{site.name}&rdquo;) are chemical
    reference materials intended solely for in-vitro laboratory research conducted by qualified
    persons. They are supplied for no other purpose.
  </p>
  <p>Our products are <strong>not</strong>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>medicinal products, and hold no marketing authorisation from the MHRA or any other regulator;</li>
    <li>food, food supplements, or nutritional products of any kind;</li>
    <li>cosmetic products intended for application to the human body;</li>
    <li>veterinary products;</li>
    <li>intended, packaged, or labelled for administration to humans or animals by any route.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    None of our products has been evaluated by any regulatory authority for safety, purity or
    efficacy in humans or animals.
  </p>

  <h2>2. No claims</h2>
  <p>
    We make no representation that any product is suitable for the diagnosis, treatment, cure or
    prevention of any condition. Where our product pages reference scientific literature, they do so
    to describe the research context in which a compound has been studied. Nothing on this website
    constitutes medical advice, a therapeutic claim, or a recommendation of use.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not supply dosing information, administration protocols, or guidance on use in humans or
    animals, and we will decline requests for such information.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Purchaser responsibilities</h2>
  <p>By placing an order you represent and warrant that:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>you are aged {site.minimumAge} or over;</li>
    <li>
      you are a qualified researcher, or are purchasing on behalf of a research institution,
      laboratory or business, and are competent to handle the materials safely;
    </li>
    <li>
      you will use the products strictly for in-vitro laboratory research and for no other purpose;
    </li>
    <li>
      you will not administer any product to yourself, to any other person, or to any animal, and
      will not supply it to any person who intends to do so;
    </li>
    <li>
      you are responsible for determining that your intended use is lawful in your jurisdiction,
      and for obtaining any authorisation, licence or ethical approval that use requires;
    </li>
    <li>
      you will handle, store, label and dispose of the materials in accordance with applicable
      health and safety legislation, including the Control of Substances Hazardous to Health
      Regulations 2002 (COSHH).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Resale and onward supply</h2>
  <p>
    You may not resell, repackage or otherwise supply our products to any third party for human or
    animal consumption, or in any manner that misrepresents them as being fit for such use. Doing so
    may constitute a criminal offence and will terminate any further supply from us.
